    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d680">

                <pb facs="0863" n="775" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg775"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">600.119/1899: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-24">December 24,
                            1918</date>.<lb/>[Received December 24—10:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4839. War Trade Board [from Sheldon]: Number 2160. Supplementing our 2067
                    December 12. Proclamation about to be issued makes trade resumption effective
                    January 1st with (1) Alsace-Lorraine and with (2) the new Italian territories
                    included in line defined by Austrian, Italian armistice of November 3d.<anchor
                        n="45" xml:id="d680-f1"/> Specific reference to Trieste and Trentino will
                    not be made.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
